      "pins": ["U44.4", "U44.5", "U48.4", "U48.5", "J17.4", "J33.4"],
      "nets": ["GND"],
      "observed": "Both sides of each isolated CAN transceiver, including GND1 and GND2, are connected to the same GND net. The CAN connectors' ground pins are on that same net.",
      "expected": "For the specified isolated CAN interfaces, the transceiver's bus-side ground should remain separate from logic-side GND; tying the grounds together bypasses the isolation barrier.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"53\") (name \"GND\") ... (node (ref \"U44\") (pin \"4\") (pinfunction \"GND1\")) (node (ref \"U44\") (pin \"5\") (pinfunction \"GND2\")) ... (node (ref \"U48\") (pin \"4\") (pinfunction \"GND1\")) (node (ref \"U48\") (pin \"5\") (pinfunction \"GND2\")) ... (node (ref \"J17\") (pin \"4\")) ... (node (ref \"J33\") (pin \"4\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "two isolated CAN buses (CAN0, CAN1), each driven ... through an isolated CAN transceiver"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The CAN interfaces do not provide galvanic isolation as specified, allowing ground-potential differences and bus-side transients to couple into the logic ground.",
      "confidence": 0.99
    },
    {
      "category": "polarity",
      "components": ["Q13", "U37", "J16"],
      "pins": ["Q13.2", "Q13.3", "Q13.1", "U37.1", "U37.6", "J16.A4", "J16.A9", "J16.B4", "J16.B9"],
      "nets": ["+5V", "NET0061", "Net-(Q13-G)"],
      "observed": "The LTC4412 path has U37.VIN on USB-C VBUS (NET0061) and U37.SENSE on +5V, but Q13's source is on +5V and its drain is on VBUS. That places the P-channel MOSFET opposite the usual input-to-output ideal-diode orientation.",
      "expected": "The ideal-diode P-channel MOSFET should be oriented for forward current from the USB input to the +5V output, with its body diode and source/drain arrangement matching the LTC4412 VIN-to-SENSE path.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"2\") (name \"+5V\") ... (node (ref \"Q13\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"S\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"83\") (name \"NET0061\") ... (node (ref \"J16\") (pin \"A4\") (pinfunction \"VBUS\")) ... (node (ref \"Q13\") (pin \"3\") (pinfunction \"D\")) ... (node (ref \"U37\") (pin \"1\") (pinfunction \"VIN\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"U37\") (pin \"6\") (pinfunction \"SENSE\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "\"LTC4412 controller and p-ch mosfet\" ... \"need reverse current protection mostly\""
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The USB input power path may fail to conduct correctly or may not provide the intended ideal-diode and reverse-current-protection behavior.",
      "confidence": 0.93
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The netlist directly defeats the specified CAN galvanic isolation by joining each transceiver's two ground domains. It also shows the LTC4412 USB ideal-diode MOSFET oriented opposite the expected input-to-output path."
}

